{
  "_schema": {
    "description": "Sample input data for Baccarat Trend-Seeker dashboard. Two top-level arrays: `tables` (static floor layout) and `hands` (hand-by-hand events). The dashboard groups hands by (table_id, minute bucket) to build per-minute animation frames.",
    "tables": {
      "id": "integer, primary key, unique within the floor",
      "label": "string, short display name e.g. 'T01'",
      "pit": "string, pit code A/B/C/D",
      "pit_label": "string, full pit name e.g. 'Pit A · Mass'",
      "x": "number, x coordinate on the floor (0 ≤ x ≤ 1400)",
      "y": "number, y coordinate on the floor (0 ≤ y ≤ 900)",
      "min": "number, table minimum bet in USD"
    },
    "hands": {
      "hand_id": "integer, globally unique sequential id",
      "table_id": "integer, foreign key → tables.id",
      "shoe_id": "integer, increments per fresh shoe at the table",
      "shoe_hand": "integer, 1-indexed position of this hand within the shoe (1..~70)",
      "hand_time": "ISO-8601 timestamp when the hand was dealt",
      "result": "string, 'B' (Banker) or 'P' (Player). Ties should be filtered out before sending.",
      "headcount": "integer 0..7, number of seated players at this hand",
      "avg_bet": "number, mean bet amount placed on this hand (USD)"
    },
    "notes": [
      "The dashboard derives the trailing trend (surprise, period, motif, broken_flag) client-side using the anchored DTP algorithm — you do NOT need to precompute those fields.",
      "Hands within the same shoe must be in chronological order. A new shoe_id resets the trailing history.",
      "If you only have hand_time and no shoe boundaries, group hands into shoes of ~70 hands each.",
      "Coordinates (x, y) only matter for the floor visualization. If you don't have a layout, use the default from utils/floorLayout.js.",
      "Tables not referenced by any hand still display on the floor (no headcount, no trend)."
    ]
  },

